{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ec0f8eb8bd7008554182f7536125822ee484bd5d00712d224bbba3befb9886e6","digest":{"component_or_area":"sync.reconverge store write lock coordination","key_entities":["sync.reconverge","src/rebar/_store/sync.py","src/rebar/_store/lock.py","check_no_rebase_in_progress","MERGE_HEAD","_do_reconverge","cindery-lithe-acaciarat","tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py::test_reconverge_waits_for_a_lock_owned_push_recovery_merge","tests/unit/test_store_sync_reconverge.py::test_reconverge_refuses_a_stranded_merge_marker_after_lock_acquisition","rebar fsck-recover"],"problem_keywords":["lock-owned merge","recovery state classification","pre-lock early exit","MERGE_HEAD marker","reconverge","misclassification","abandoned recovery","push recovery merge"],"propositions":["sync.reconverge checks recovery state before acquiring the store write lock, causing it to misclassify a transient MERGE_HEAD created by the lock-owning push recovery merge as an abandoned recovery state.","A peer process calling sync.reconverge emits an fsck-recover warning and returns without waiting for the lock when the lock holder is still executing its push recovery merge.","Recovery state classification must be authoritative only after the store write lock is acquired, while fetch remains outside the lock.","A stranded merge marker found after lock acquisition must still block reset or merge mutation and direct the operator to rebar fsck-recover via the in-lock check_no_rebase_in_progress guard."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787944705959642259,"uuid":"da